# React UI

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| Type | Rule |
| Audience | Developer when editing UI |
| Adapt | Narrow `globs` in the frontmatter to this repository's UI packages. |

- Functional components only. Match the export style of the file you are in.
- Colocate feature state with existing context or store patterns. Do not add
  a new state library unless the specification requires it.
- New user-facing screens need a route **and** an accessible name.
- User-visible strings: keep the tone of the current application; no secrets
  in the client.
- States: implement empty, loading, and error when the specification names
  them. Do not leave a blank screen on failure.
- Accessibility: keep skip links, `aria-label` on icon-only controls, and
  real `<button>` / `<a>` (not clickable `div`s).
- Do not use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or `bypassSecurityTrust*`. Encode
  dynamic text via React children.
- Styles: reuse existing CSS classes; do not drop in a new CSS framework for
  one screen.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<div onClick={go}>Cart</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<NavLink to="/cart" className="cart-link" aria-label={`Cart with ${count} items`}>
  Bag
</NavLink>
```
